\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For a finitely generated free group F and injective endomorphism $\varphi :F\to F$, if the ascending HNN extension $\langle F,t|t^{-1}ft=\varphi (f)$, $f\in F\rangle $ is word-hyperbolic, must it be virtually compact special?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For a finitely generated free group F and injective endomorphism $\varphi :F\to F$, if the ascending HNN extension $\langle F,t|t^{-1}ft=\varphi (f)$, $f\in F\rangle $ is word-hyperbolic, must it be virtually compact special?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{http://aimpl.org/freebycyclic/3/}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Virtual-compact-specialness-of-hyperbolic-one-relator-groups-September-25-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

