\section*{Virtual compact specialness of hyperbolic ascending free-group mapping tori}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Every hyperbolic one-relator group is claimed virtually compact special and, by the cited theorem, virtually free-by-cyclic with possibly infinitely generated free kernel.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Primitive-extension reduction and a filling criterion organize progressive characters and walls. The resulting cubulation and hierarchy meet the virtual-specialness criterion; the free-by-cyclic consequence is then imported from the established special-group result.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The additional theorem concerns the mapping torus formed from an injective endomorphism of a free group of finite rank. Assuming that torus is hyperbolic, it is claimed virtually compact special, which gives the question in its specified mapping-torus setting. This is presented as a claimed affirmative answer.

\subsection{Formal verification}
